Hi:

I'd like to add a simple R console with an entry and a text area my
application (My application visualizes multiple runs and parameter sweeps
for NetLogo models, will be GPL, etc ...)
I looked at code in JGRConsole, biocept, walware, and other places and I
still can't figure it out.

I studied the rtest2 example but I am at a loss on how to change the input
from stdin to an entry (JTextField).
Basically I can't think of how to block in rReadConsole from a JTextField ?.
(Additionally, I am worried on how to do it right since I have a JavaGD
device that I want to keep refreshing)

Specifically, I am confused by who must handle the event loop:
     - Do you have to block in rReadConsole ?
     - Can you start the event from a actionPerformed callback ?
Below is an rtest3 example where I just added a JTextField to use as an
entry, but got stuck. :-(

Additionally, please let me know if any self contained R Console widget
exists, I googled it forever but could not find any ...


                Thanks for the nice Java/R interface.

                                           Daniel.


